    {/* ——— the rules ——— */}
    <section class="band band-sky" id="rules">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">The rules</p>
        <h2>Things that are always true</h2>
        <div class="two-up">
          <div class="rule-list card">
            <h3><Icon name="heart-kind" /> Always</h3>
            <ul class="flow">
              <li>Every Gritty starts from a drawing Kim made.</li>
              <li>Warm paper, never stark white.</li>
              <li>Gritty looks at his speech bubble.</li>
              <li>Speech bubbles are handwritten; nothing else is.</li>
              <li>Every feeling is okay, and mistakes are lucky.</li>
              <li>Text is big, buttons are big, and anything that moves can be
              paused.</li>
              <li>Colours on top of colours are checked for contrast — ink or
              deep blue on the bright grounds.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-list card">
            <h3><Icon name="feeling-worried" /> Never</h3>
            <ul class="flow">
              <li>Never a Gritty invented from a description. Nothing “in
              the style of” without one of Kim’s drawings as the
              source.</li>
              <li>Never collect anything from a child: no forms, no sign-ups,
              no cookies.</li>
              <li>Never gold for decoration — it means something was
              achieved.</li>
              <li>Never white lettering on gold, green, pink or sky.</li>
              <li>Never informational text smaller than the floor.</li>
              <li>Never shame. No “wrong”, no red X, no sad trombone.</li>
              <li>Never flip a drawing in software to face the other way —
              it flips his eyes too.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

